      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Why can a reseller rank on my own brand name? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Because Google rewards the page best optimised for the query, not the product's owner. A reseller with an older domain and structured product pages can get ahead. It's a technical gap, so it's closeable.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Can you request a knowledge panel from Google? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>You don't request it, you earn it. It appears when Google clearly understands your brand as an entity: a consistent name everywhere, structured data, presence on recognised sources, assets linked together.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">How long to take back my branded SERP? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>On branded queries it's generally faster than on category queries, because competition is low and the demand is already there. A diagnostic prioritises the quickest wins first.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

